---
title: "How does a reader tell which calendar a row came from?"
accTitle: "Calendar identity stack"
accDescr: "Config stores the Google id and a unique label. The journal keys by id. The vault row, list column, and painter all show the same label."
config:
  flowchart:
    rankSpacing: 16
    nodeSpacing: 16
    wrappingWidth: 240
---
flowchart TB
  subgraph CONFIG["Config"]
    direction TB
    ID["`**id**<br/>Google calendar id`"]
    LABEL["`**label**<br/>Birthdays`"]
  end
  subgraph WRITE["bob gcal sync"]
    direction TB
    KEY["`**Journal key**<br/>id plus event id`"]
    ROW["`**Vault row**<br/>[cal:: Birthdays]`"]
  end
  subgraph READ["Readers"]
    direction TB
    LIST["`**bob gcal list**<br/>CAL column`"]
    PAINT["`**Ledger painter**<br/>green Birthdays chip`"]
  end
  ID ==> KEY
  LABEL ==> ROW
  KEY --> ROW
  ROW ==> LIST
  ROW ==> PAINT
  classDef focus fill:#E8F1FB,stroke:#3B78C2,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#0F2E52
  classDef outcome fill:#E7F5EC,stroke:#2E7D4F,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#123D24
  classDef muted fill:#F3F4F6,stroke:#6B7280,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#1F2937
  class ID,LABEL focus
  class KEY muted
  class ROW,LIST,PAINT outcome
  style CONFIG fill:none,stroke:#3B78C2
  style WRITE fill:none,stroke:#6B7280
  style READ fill:none,stroke:#2E7D4F
